# What ships is decided by the `files` allowlist in package.json, which names
# `dist/**/*.js` and `dist/**/*.d.ts` — an allowlist npm applies before this
# file is consulted, and one this file cannot widen.
#
# So this exists for two narrower jobs:
#
# 1. It stops `.gitignore` being read as the ignore list. npm falls back to it
#    when this file is absent, and `.gitignore` lists `dist` — the one
#    directory that has to ship.
# 2. It is the second gate on anything added to `files` later: a broadened
#    allowlist still will not sweep up tests, fixtures or notes.
#
# Source maps are excluded by the allowlist rather than here. `src` is not
# published, so a shipped map points at files that are not in the tarball:
# worse than no map, and two thirds of the unpacked size.

# Tests and fixtures.
test/
tests/
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.js
**/__fixtures__/
**/fixtures/

# Sources and build tooling. Only the compiled output ships.
src/
tsconfig*.json
vitest.config.ts
.claude/

# Project notes that are not the README.
Claude.md
CLAUDE.md
